{"id":"wikibooks:baked-penne","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3ABaked_Penne","status":"fixed","reason":"Restore conversion template measurements and oven temperatures.","ingredients":["1 cup (125 g) uncooked penne pasta","1 cup (300 g) ricotta cheese","4 eggs, separated and at room temperature","¼ cup (½ stick/125 g) unsalted butter, melted","⅛ tsp cream of tartar","1 pinch salt","¼ tsp freshly ground black pepper","1 tsp minced garlic","1 tbsp finely chopped flat-leaf parsley","½ cup (60 g) grated mozzarella cheese","1½ cups (400 g) tomato paste","4 fresh basil leaves"],"steps":["Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).","Cook pasta in a gallon of salted boiling water until al dente. Drain, rinse with cold water and set aside.","Combine ricotta, egg yolks, butter, salt, pepper, garlic, parsley and tomato paste. Fold in pasta.","Beat egg whites with cream of tartar in a spotlessly clean metal bowl to stiff peaks. Gently fold into pasta mixture.","Pour into a parchment-lined high-sided roasting pan. Sprinkle with mozzarella, cover with foil and bake in the center of the oven for 15 minutes.","Remove foil and lower oven to 350°F (175°C). Bake another 30 minutes until browned and bubbly.","Plate portions, garnish with basil and serve warm."]}]}
